{"situation": "I know that change CHG-1, raised by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved, will lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove an inbound route filter on core site A, with sandbox stage skipped and rollback plan available; it is scheduled to apply in 3 minutes. I do not know whether the change has been risk-assessed or why the sandbox stage was skipped, and I do not have evidence of any personal-data impact assessment or regulator approval.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is auto-approved, skips the sandbox stage, and is scheduled to apply in 3 minutes on core site A.",
        "rule": "A network change that lowers route-flood protection and removes an inbound route filter can trigger protect-mode or mass outage, as seen in the FCC report; the NOC mandate includes rollback_change to restore the previous snapshot.",
        "inference": "To prevent a likely service outage before 3 minutes elapse, I should restore the previous configuration snapshot for CHG-1."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "It took close to two hours to roll back the network change. Full service restoration, however, took at least 12 hours because AT&T Mobility’s device registration systems were overwhelmed with the high volume of requests for re-registration onto the network."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no mandatory rule or owner ensuring that closed-loop network optimisation changes cannot reach production after a skipped sandbox stage.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The inject shows CHG-1 was auto-approved with the field 'sandbox stage': skipped.",
        "rule": "Global standards describe an ML sandbox as part of efficient management of multi-level ML mechanisms, and a comparable misconfigured change produced a nationwide outage.",
        "inference": "A control gap allows a high-risk network change to be auto-approved without mandatory sandbox validation or human review."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "Taking into account the nature, scope and purposes of data processing, the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk to the privacy and confidentiality of the Data Subject's Personal Data."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025", "quote": "ML pipeline along with MLFO and ML sandbox [ITU-T Y.3172] allows an efficient management of multi-level ML mechanism in operator's network."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "I know from NOC that OpCo's CHG-1 rollback failed with 'ValueError: no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', and that CHG-1 was auto-approved with sandbox skipped and scheduled to apply in 3 minutes. I do not yet know the actual service impact, affected services, or whether emergency calls are affected.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "open_incident",
      "params": {
        "topic": "CHG-1 rollback failure at OpCo"
      },
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-MSG02"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports CHG-1 rollback failed: ValueError: no applied change CHG-1 to roll back. CHG-1 was auto-approved with sandbox skipped and scheduled to apply in 3 minutes.",
        "rule": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000 grants TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by licensees.",
        "inference": "A failed network change with potential service impact falls within TDRA's regulatory oversight, so opening an incident record is appropriate."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_report",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC",
        "topic": "CHG-1 failure: current service impact, affected services, timeline and rollback status"
      },
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-MSG02"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC states service impact is being assessed and the rollback failed.",
        "rule": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000 gives TDRA authority to regulate service conditions, level and scope.",
        "inference": "TDRA needs timely information from the licensee to assess the incident and any consumer protection implications."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_audit",
      "params": {
        "of": "NOC",
        "topic": "CHG-1 auto-approval and sandbox skip"
      },
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-MSG02"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was auto-approved with sandbox skipped, and rollback failed.",
        "rule": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000 authorises TDRA to regulate service standards and quality.",
        "inference": "TDRA should examine the licensee's testing and change records to determine whether the change management process was adequate."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-TDRA-CPR-2#0000",
          "quote": "grants the TDRA the power to issue regulations, instructions, decisions and rules regulating the conditions, level and scope of services provided by the Licensees to subscribers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_direction",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "direction": "Prioritise service continuity and assess the CHG-1 failure; do not apply further unverified changes until the failed rollback and service impact are resolved."
      },
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-MSG02"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was scheduled to apply in 3 minutes and the rollback failed.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019 requires the licensee to provide and maintain service coverage in accordance with the TDRA's Regulatory Framework.",
        "inference": "TDRA can direct the licensee to take immediate resilience and continuity measures to protect service coverage."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall deploy and roll out its Telecommunication Network and related Services and provide and maintain service coverage in accordance with the TDRA’s Regulatory Framework."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No UAE text in the provided excerpts requires peer review or sandbox execution before a network change is auto-approved.",
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-MSG02"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was auto-approved with sandbox skipped.",
        "rule": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019 generally requires deployment in accordance with the TDRA's Regulatory Framework, but does not specify peer review or sandbox controls.",
        "inference": "There is a regulatory gap on mandatory pre-change technical safeguards for network changes."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall deploy and roll out its Telecommunication Network and related Services and provide and maintain service coverage in accordance with the TDRA’s Regulatory Framework."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0018",
          "quote": "Adequate peer review should have prevented the network change from being approved, and, in turn, from being loaded onto the network. This peer review did not take place."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "We know CHG-1 was auto-approved, skipped sandbox, and was scheduled to lower route-flood protection and remove the inbound route filter on core site A; core A has now isolated, R2 has call-setup failures, 6 of 15 sites are unserved, and emergency-call routing has no path while core B is healthy. We do not know why rollback_change returned 'no applied change CHG-1' or whether the change fully applied.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "wilt_sites",
      "params": {
        "region": "R2"
      },
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-I2"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-I2 reports core site A isolated after route count exceeded protection limit, 6 of 15 R2 cell sites unserved, and no emergency-call routing path; core B is healthy with spare capacity.",
        "rule": "The emergency call service is a fundamental legal obligation; wilt_sites moves a region's cell sites off a failed core onto a working core.",
        "inference": "Moving R2 cell sites to core B can restore call-setup and emergency-call routing."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000",
          "quote": "Giving access to the emergency call service is not optional, it is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility telecommunications providers have"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": [
        "REG",
        "EMS"
      ],
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-I2"
      ],
      "statement": "S1-I2 alarm: core site A isolated; R2 call-setup failures spike; 6 of 15 cell sites unserved; emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path; core site B healthy."
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The retrieved UAE knowledge contains no explicit rule requiring sandbox testing and verified rollback before an auto-approved closed-loop network change can lower route-flood protection and remove an inbound route filter.",
      "inject_refs": [
        "S1-I1",
        "S1-FB01",
        "S1-I2"
      ],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was auto-approved with sandbox stage skipped and rollback later failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'; the core then isolated on route count.",
        "rule": "UAE data protection law requires a pre-deployment impact assessment for high-risk modern technologies, but no retrieved UAE operational-resilience rule imposes analogous sandbox/rollback verification for autonomous network changes.",
        "inference": "There is a standards gap for automated core network change safety."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066",
          "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk to the privacy and confidentiality of the Data Subject's Personal Data."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000",
          "quote": "The ACMA will not hesitate to take strong enforcement action where alleged telco failures have jeopardised public access to the critical emergency call service"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "R2 emergency-call routing and site serving have been restored after wilt_sites moved R2 onto core B, but core site A is still isolated and the CHG-1 rollback failed. I do not know whether any regulatory emergency notification is required for this unplanned outage or whether EMS/REG have been informed.",
